  "definitions": {
    "X12": "SENSORARRAY_CELL_ERROR_UNSTABLE=18: fresh CRC-accepted sample set fails the5000uV spread test. It is not a route fault or a valid voltage.",
    "X02": "SENSORARRAY_CELL_ERROR_SPI=2 is also the compatible wire code for a locally exhausted CRC retry. The first successful sample can leave acquired/fresh set even when later samples fail; valid remains clear.",
    "pga=0": "PGA bypass, not gain zero or missing channel.",
    "fresh_vs_valid": "Fresh/acquired records a completed contemporary conversion. The separate valid bit and Xhh token control scientific usability.",
    "unknown_sentinel": "LastGoodKnown=0 makes4294967295 an unavailable sentinel, not a measured multi-year age."
  },
  "review_conclusions": [
    "The recorded X12 points are all S1D2/PGA bypass; they remain invalid without invented zero values. The recordings do not identify whether the physical cause is floating input, settling, source noise or another analog effect.",
    "The ordinary value/pga cache cannot ingest rejected CRC data. The fresh-read wrapper also requires current physical/configuration generation and a new DRDY/NEW_DATA result; later timeout/configuration failures remain fatal rather than being waived as CRC.",
    "A separate PGA-only cache-stability defect was confirmed and fixed with an executed production-function regression; it is not attributed to these recorded bypass X12 points. See ads-stability-fix-review.json.",
    "External rail calibration remains explicit configuration, not a time-refreshed internal measurement. Its AINCOM midpoint remains estimated and uncertainty unknown. Neither large frame age nor valid ADC point proves absolute voltage accuracy or correct source loading.",
    "No rail refresh appears in these capture receipt windows. The board reports no isolated internal rail-monitor capability; CAP/VOLT paths cannot use a transparent INTREF-on monitor. Observed battery POWER/INTREF records stay INTREF=0 and matched saved/restored core pairs agree. This is register evidence, not an oscilloscope measurement of isolation.",
    "Battery valid runs increased116/120 with no new invalid runs or restore failures in the query windows. The earlier rail_invalid state did not fabricate a last-good sample.",
    "Observed periodic register-health reads remain at engine interval64 and include many cumulative512 boundaries across a nonzero mode-entry count. Diagnostic logs are not claimed complete.",
    "Runtime driver CRC rate exceeds2.5% in the USB-only observed health window (about3.71%). Boot qualification must not replace this runtime evidence; this remains a separate acceptance/diagnosis item."
  ],
  "acceptable_scope": "Invalid-point semantics and bounded error isolation can be accepted from these records and executed regressions. Do not accept absolute analog accuracy, unknown-input interpretation, zero runtime CRC errors, or the new unflashed PGA repair as HIL-verified.",
  "known_blocker_status": {
    "PGA_cache": "Fixed in source and host regression; root target/HIL integration pending.",
    "runtime_crc_over_user_tolerance": "Unresolved. Exact counter/byte/timing qualification analysis requested next; no threshold or clock change made by this review."
  }
}
